#: ../../reference/files.rst:2 fd3b7967bb874d57b65462c88411d2e3
msgid "Files, printing and packaging"
msgstr "File, stampa e pacchettizzazione"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:7 95b5770cc0154d1daa085c1cef2c8dfd
msgid "Storage"
msgstr "Archiviazione"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:9 02c27900858749c18dc405f07fdc87ff
msgid ""
"One folder per competition. Everything the jury makes is in it, and it "
"copies to a memory stick at the end of the day."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:27 2d2cc6df51b24c8b8707cb22f10b1577
msgid ""
"The root is ``competitions/`` in a checkout and ``Documents\\BlueBand`` when"
" installed, overridden by ``COMMISSAIRE_TRACK_DATA`` either way. Competition"
" folders are the jury's work and stay out of the repository — the one "
"exception is ``competitions/example/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:33 7ed9da95b9064be1aec85221c49e0389
msgid "Nothing is lost"
msgstr "Niente si perde"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:35 d22ac70288a74f609e619dad4b4dc577
msgid ""
"Every write is atomic — temp file plus ``os.replace`` — and keeps the "
"previous content as a snapshot. Nothing typed by the jury can be lost by a "
"crash, a bad edit or a browser reload."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:47 95a5831b498646b5b4b94af9115b5293
msgid ""
"``journal.jsonl`` is append-only and never rewritten: one line per write, "
"with the action, the target and the time. It is what answers *what happened "
"at 14:30* — including why a PDF came out as HTML."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:51 4be7c2c2a8cb4549a6e8cf7a89bc5666
msgid ""
"``races/<race_id>.json`` is a ``RaceState``, and everything a format needs "
"lives in its ``payload``. The race id is ``race.race_key(cat, event, "
"round_key)``, and round keys are the strings written in ``programme.yaml`` —"
" which is why translating a round name would orphan its race file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:56 9428023ab7494b36a22f4f51a8a96bb0
msgid ""
"``settings.json`` holds the choices of *this machine and this competition*: "
"``language``, ``out_dir``, ``use_overlay``, the letterhead in progress, and "
"various UI keys. Anything that is a statement about the **competition** — "
"what a team is, the entry-file layout, the branding — lives in "
"``programme.yaml``, not here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:63 0050f88422ac405f9d3e4fec011fc263
msgid "``core.paths``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:65 0d7deafe68de41bd804f22ffb6787a19
msgid ""
"Run from the repository, every path answers with the repository. Installed, "
"two different places, and conflating them is how a jury loses a "
"championship."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:68 fdb7087b4d424430803cfbede3b3b946
msgid "``bundle()``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:69 7f5f2a0d630b4a7983caebf16e36ab82
msgid ""
"**What the program is** — regulations, templates, stylesheet. Read-only, "
"replaced wholesale by the next version, and under PyInstaller it lives in "
"``sys._MEIPASS``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:73 b246cfc9359b462495f5440906b777c7
msgid "``data()``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:74 c34ac1d35fb74d39aa130bbcf0fc114b
msgid ""
"**What the jury made** — competitions, results, communiqués. It must outlive"
" an uninstall, be findable without a file manager, and be easy to copy to a "
"stick, so it goes in the user's Documents and never inside the installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:78 564697ec2d7e4247b2d0aa675f34c181
msgid "``served()``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:79 17a762d15e814e14a2394e2e226cf5df
msgid ""
"The copies of the last saved PDFs that Streamlit serves out of ``static/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:81 352fd58a266d430eb7ffd6d3d078f084
msgid ""
"``core.paths`` is the only module that knows any of this, which is why "
"nothing else in the codebase had to learn about ``sys._MEIPASS``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:88 bc7944874ec945c59d1f79753b02e036
msgid "Regulation files"
msgstr "I file del regolamento"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:90 f19c30517a9848c59d21c8630b8d1c5a
msgid ""
"Eight JSON tables under ``regulations/``. **The regulation is data, not "
"code**: a rule that changes next year is a file edit, and none of it needs a"
" release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:93 f99255c81bb440dfbc8bc30ebe06980d
msgid ""
"Two kinds live here, maintained differently: **ours**, written by the app as"
" well as read by it (``distances.json``, ``events.json``, "
"``categories.json``, ``notes.json``, ``communiques.json``, "
"``entry_formats.json``); and **theirs**, read-only and replaced wholesale by"
" a newer version (``penalties.json`` from the UCI, ``PUIS.json`` from the "
"federation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:103 81db3231014946cca1d2975170476cae
msgid "File"
msgstr "File"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:104 be2d619c6c664d83b4518e4356c14015
msgid "Read by"
msgstr "Letto da"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:105 f3d5bfcce8d94aa49326bcb7c6c25c39
msgid "What it holds"
msgstr "Che cosa contiene"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:106 0e1e8cb89c6d4f6eb00220a5b89d19b9
