msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:107 ../../reference/files.rst:111
#: 0e4c3c7e21314aaf937e3e15f533dfb3 55798c6a3e4e4a55b512aaeb5b9beb92
msgid "``core.catalogue``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:108 b14bd7bf288445858a9936050985e310
msgid ""
"What an event *is*: code, name per language, UCI abbreviation, format, "
"riders per team, how many start together, the entry-column headings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:110 edb35c82069f46bea18c1b908fe3c10c
msgid "``categories.json``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:112 ce072a11c5054c57854aecdbc83c3f28
msgid "The standard category codes, with sex and name per language."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:113 655dd72751d3481585fb27fef7296ab0
msgid "``distances.json``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:114 d7cdbba0b53c452ea0387fbce243896f
msgid "``core.distances``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:115 b0e8ef0339134c458401b9112270c283
msgid "How long a race is, how often it sprints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:116 59f802c456bf4783b79235a2f92e7cad
msgid "``entry_formats.json``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:117 8d2866d669d7487491bdfac6e980a7fe
msgid "``core.entry_formats``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:118 4a3fbf9dcba140bb96237f4be7d06b91
msgid "How each shape of entry file is read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:119 ce7d26ce1f4b4c568cc9dff7372a2df3
msgid "``notes.json``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:120 55c27601549741e1b4e30c3b7f077ca3
msgid "``core.notes``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:121 df806d0d2b984d788d6e2615fee2019c
msgid "Which regulation line opens which sheet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:122 b3b98e9e335541ddac793bcae1f8d345
msgid "``communiques.json``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:123 3c6d13e922794de8bbb6b7f6f6a676e3
msgid "``core.communiques``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:124 7cef13b40838410b98571976bd38aab5
msgid "Which sheets share a number, per format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:125 9847b734a7ac444c825cb0317fa35307
msgid "``penalties.json``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:126 ../../reference/files.rst:130
#: 3822e0bb78284510a13736b43989f242 69d90df4e5344e6fa351dd69ad3d8c9d
msgid "``core.decisions``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:127 910255a3dcfb464097465e1e1d23541b
msgid ""
"The UCI wording of track offences, in four languages, numbered as the UCI "
"numbers them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:129 8121d07ee53b4788a05e5b2fc16e7a23
msgid "``PUIS.json``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:131 a5b507a8b9454cbc8ef376630094c153
msgid "The federal table of what each infringement costs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:133 1ca9716450a7448095a89e86080210b8
msgid ""
"Every file carries ``_last_updated_``, and most carry ``_about_``. Neither "
"is read by the code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:136 79446b1b30f1482680a7028efe628dc5
msgid ""
"The **name of an event is per language**, because it is not a label: it is "
"written into ``programme.yaml`` and printed on the sheets exactly as it "
"stands there. Adding an event to an English competition writes the English "
"name, and it prints in English next year too, whoever opens the file. An "
"event the table does not know is still declared by hand in the programme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:142 41da380120bd4193b7bc2a009eac10bb
msgid ""
"Distances are matched loosely on three levels — **event → category → "
"round**. A round is looked up by its own name first, then by the family it "
"belongs to, then by ``*``. Nothing here is invented: the file ships seeded "
"from a programme that was actually run, and an event the table says nothing "
"about proposes no distance at all — a blank field on the page rather than a "
"wrong number on a sheet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:148 528e29711eac4eeab4eb9f229b4cc816
msgid ""
"``notes.json`` holds two things. **Which line goes on which sheet** is "
"``rules``, and it ships filled in, because it is the regulation — one rule "
"per sentence, naming the format, the round, the document and the condition. "
"**The numbers are the programme's**: a rule names the field it reads, and "
"the placeholder is filled from the round as the jury typed it. ``texts`` is "
"the installation's own wording of any catalogue entry, and it ships empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:159 277ca90bc65d434e921b109532055bc7
msgid "Printing"
msgstr "Stampa"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:161 7eb603308cc34aa9b4d0bbd91e2caa0a
msgid "One pipeline for every sheet the app produces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:179 3cbfd06cbe0a476782a0f413b34950cd
msgid ""
"**``w`` is a weight, not a width.** The table normalises its columns' "
"weights to percentages summing to 100, so no sheet can starve a column into "
"a two-character sliver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:183 efc04b7a5b16474089db3f9b50a1f8de
msgid ""
"**``min_mm`` is the one thing a weight cannot express**: how narrow a column"
" may actually get *on paper*. A name that loses its last letters is still a "
"name; ``DNF`` truncated to ``DN…`` and a UCI ID missing two digits are not "
"the thing they are printed for. Those columns declare the millimetres they "
"need and the table gives them, out of what the others were sharing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:189 899ae24941e544ae82d5374ab31e9186
msgid ""
"**Notes are tinted by kind.** A disqualification and \"the first two go "
"through to the final\" are both prose in a box, and they are not the same "
"thing: one is a sanction a team may appeal, the other is how the tournament "
"is run. The plain note prints last and keeps its grey, because a colour on "
"it would say somebody had been sanctioned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:195 b856778ab5564f919fb0cffa64038df6
msgid ""
"**Landscape is opt-in, never automatic.** Chrome does not repeat a table "
"header group across the pages of a named page, so a landscape communiqué "
"loses its letterhead on every continuation sheet — the one thing these "
"documents must not lose."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:200 dc7245a279474aff8375e692d3f42786
msgid ""
"The sheets carry a full-width letterhead and footer repeated on every page —"
" they are the ``thead`` and ``tfoot`` of one table, which is how a browser "
"repeats them. Around the table, six slots, each holding one of "
"``communique``, ``printed_at`` or nothing; an element lives in one place, so"
" putting it elsewhere removes it from where it was. A provisional sheet "
"(``draft=True``) prints a \"not final\" box where the number goes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:207 85255eee78244c9597d6e51f5e4dd8b8
msgid ""
"``render/print.css`` is one file used in two places: inlined into the "
"standalone page that Chromium prints, and injected into the Streamlit app so"
" the previews look like the sheet. Everything in it is scoped to ``.cmsr`` "
"except the ``@media print`` block, which hides the sidebar and the toolbar "
"when the jury prints straight from the browser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:215 2da243bb79b3482a978a3842d78949b7
msgid ""
"The CSS goes in through ``st.markdown``, not ``st.html``: the latter "
"sanitises what it is handed and throws away its ``<style>``. The same "
"sanitiser drops the whole SVG namespace, which is why the derny charts are "
"drawn with ``st.markdown`` too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:220 d0eacaea81ce4a1baf760432f6704590
msgid ""
"``render/pdf.py`` runs a headless Chromium — the same engine the jury would "
"print with by hand, so the PDF is what the browser's own print produces "
"minus its date and URL header. No extra Python dependency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:224 929d4c458fca44d38a5a4d3b3c1d15ba
msgid ""
"**Where Chromium works is not where the document ends up.** The browser has "
"to *read* the page and *write* the PDF, and a sandboxed Chromium can do "
"neither under ``/tmp`` nor on the network mount the communiqués folder "
"usually is. So ``work_dirs`` tries the caller's directory first, then local "
"candidates, and only the finished bytes are written to the destination. A "
"directory that has worked once goes to the front — printing a whole day must"
" not pay for the same failed attempt on every sheet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:232 299dd6e425ae47d2969b7f96f0a3b130
msgid ""
"``out_name`` produces ``018_classification_madison_final.pdf`` — the "
"communiqué number, then a slug of the title."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:235 78455922d3fa4a678f97540959c9d779
msgid ""
"``render/markup.py`` is four constructs of markdown — headings, bold, "
"italic, code, bullets, numbers, a rule, paragraphs — for the one place in "
"the app that takes prose rather than a field. **Everything is escaped before"
" anything is read.** What the jury types is text, never markup: a sheet that"
" renders an ``<img>`` somebody pasted into the box is a sheet that can be "
"made to say anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:246 462d588bc5cf45958276b901cf50abd3
msgid "Translations"
msgstr "Traduzioni"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:248 e9e89f3e148e4dffbdf142fc7bac30c6
msgid ""
"The code speaks UCI English — competition, event, round, bib, club, region. "
"What reaches a screen or a printed sheet is a **lookup, never a literal**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:260 86ae89c7d3bd455f8f2fac4d658d3e72
msgid ""
"Nothing under ``core/``, ``render/`` or ``ui/`` writes prose of its own. "
"Adding a language is adding one module and listing it in ``CATALOGUES``; "
"correcting a wording is editing one entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:264 6c03540a6c5746c391c41575fa692a4c
msgid ""
"Each catalogue defines the same dictionaries, named by what they name: "
"``FIELDS`` (a column of the entry list), ``RACE`` (a column or word of a "
"race sheet), ``DOCS`` (a kind of document), ``STATUSES`` and "
"``STATUS_NAMES`` (the result codes as printed and spelled out), "
"``PENALTIES``, ``NOTE_KINDS``, ``CODES``, ``UI``, ``HELP`` and ``MSG``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:270 1b49388d31014aa4adce6eee52c53282
msgid ""
"``label(key)`` does **not** raise on an unknown key — it comes back "
"capitalised, so a new column still shows up readable. ``ui``, ``msg`` and "
"``help_text`` do: a missing control label is a bug to fix, not a word to "
"invent. A key the language in force does not have is answered from the "
"default catalogue, which is a good deal better than an empty widget or a "
"``KeyError`` at the track."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:276 209963c088924abcbf9993ddb615020b
msgid ""
"The language is **per competition**, chosen in the settings and set once per"
" rerun before anything draws a word. It moves the **catalogue only**: what "
"``programme.yaml`` spells out — the names of the categories, the events and "
"the rounds — prints as it is written there, in any language. Those strings "
"are also the keys races are stored under."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:282 8bf1dda14728404c946e4f6e389b282b
msgid ""
"To add a language: copy an existing catalogue, translate the values keeping "
"every key, set ``NAME``, and add it to ``CATALOGUES``. "
"``tests/test_i18n.py`` then checks that every key the app asks for exists, "
"that every language answers all of them **with the same placeholders**, and "
"that no module outside ``core/i18n/`` writes prose of its own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:288 88d77fd9f63c426fa95ef916a93ff52e
msgid ""
"The abbreviations a printed sheet uses are the **UCI** ones — see the "
":ref:`glossary`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:295 e974382fc0a54d829cd16de312af99c0
msgid "Windows build"
msgstr "La build per Windows"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:297 7684509345d447528fcc19869db99606
msgid "The console ships as an ``.exe`` a jury installs by double-clicking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:305 d9f64f4b4c2a49f1b2dd183eceac1dd7
msgid ""
"Out comes ``dist/BlueBand-<version>-setup.exe``. CI does the same on every "
"``v*`` tag and attaches it to the release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:309 c52e66fe79044f6c984f85600ffa5287
msgid "What it weighs, and why"
msgstr "Quanto pesa, e perché"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:311 84e58e6600884169bb23720107756a71
msgid ""
"The app installs at **about 435 MB**, and most of that is three packages the"
" console never imports by name: pandas, numpy and pyarrow (~334 MB), "
"Streamlit and its dependencies (~87 MB), CPython and the bootloader (~20 "
"MB). The app itself, with its regulations and templates, is about 1 MB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:316 fca1ebb1daf14cf48b226a2e3dce2a08
msgid ""
"They are there because ``st.dataframe`` and ``st.data_editor`` are made of "
"them. **This was measured, and the alternative was built and rejected**: "
"hand-written HTML tables brought the installation down to 108 MB and were "
"worse to use — rows twice as tall, a select too narrow to read, and none of "
"the sorting, resizing, full screen, search and copy that come free. Keep "
"that in mind before \"optimising\" the dependency list: the size is a "
"decision that has already been taken, once, with numbers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:325 dcf97311cd604e3dab52b7b26edb55a8
msgid "The three awkward things about freezing Streamlit"
msgstr "Le tre scomodità del congelare Streamlit"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:327 e89568430aee4fb09a3f260f1bc684b5
msgid ""
"All three are solved in ``packaging/blueband.spec``, and each was a build "
"that succeeded and then failed at runtime:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:330 0f91e958524349c89966b18893d0123b
msgid ""
"**Streamlit reads its own version from its installed metadata.** Without the"
" ``.dist-info`` in the bundle it raises at import — ``copy_metadata``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:332 1df8a5c6d7ae4e408ca1691b9408d6e4
msgid ""
"**Its frontend is data.** ``streamlit/static/`` is the compiled React app — "
"``collect_data_files``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:334 edd0523bffbd4ac6a25702a9e05e9342
msgid ""
"**The app is never imported.** The analysis starts at ``launcher.py``, which"
" hands Streamlit ``app.py`` as a *path*, so ``core``, ``ui`` and ``render`` "
"are in no import graph: the bundle starts, serves a page, and dies on ``No "
"module named 'core'`` at the first render. ``collect_submodules``, with the "
"repository put on ``sys.path`` first — without that it finds nothing and "
"returns an empty list **with only a warning**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:341 75b5711cc7ff48559fa6c4091fa35dd5
msgid ""
"``BlueBand.exe --check`` is the guard against all three: it imports every "
"module and looks for every data file, and it fails at the door instead of on"
" the jury's first click."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:345 b5265ebc7e72437c943efe84afc80a2b
msgid ""
"The install is **per-user on purpose**, twice over: no administrator prompt "
"on a laptop nobody has the password for, and the program's folder stays "
"writable — Streamlit serves the last saved PDFs out of ``static/`` inside "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:350 8be6118789d143589905f5ac63f977e4
msgid "Building on Linux"
msgstr "Costruirlo su Linux"

#: ../../reference/files.rst:352 5a48fdf81b904bf488965da4b4c45fde
msgid ""
"The whole recipe except the ``.ico`` and the installer works on Linux, and "
"that is worth doing before pushing a tag:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/files.rst:361 e3a9551c8f954936b7a031d6265109d0
msgid ""
"Build it in a **clean virtual environment**, never in a working scientific "
"one: PyInstaller bundles what it finds, and the ``excludes`` in the spec are"
" a safety net rather than a guarantee."
msgstr ""
